This task is to delete the bagheera_reboot_token_file.bin file which is present in /dev/shm/
A ramfile with the name "bagheera_reboot_token_file.bin" is created in the shared memory space whenever bagheera service is started for the first time after device reboot.
This file is intentionally created to differentiate between “bagheera start after device reboot” and “bagheera start without device reboot (on account of camera crash, segmentation fault or force restart)”.
This ramfile should be deleted whenever there is an ota  update. This is needed to mimic the “bagheera start after device reboot” scenario.
